  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 296705,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/AJ-comp/Compiler",
  "published": "2026-10-19T03:57:10.137Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Janglim 0.4.0 adds typed EBNF token declarations, leading source trivia and line-break metadata, and host-registered C# predicates using {Name()}? syntax. Two-way Shift/predicate epsilon Reduce conflicts use on-demand lookahead with explicit failure, ambiguity, and resource-limit diagnostics. Grammar validation rejects input-free repetition and predicate-bearing zero-token left recursion while preserving ordinary LR left recursion. LALRParser remains the supported path, with the existing 0.x API policy. Full release notes: https://github.com/AJ-comp/Compiler/blob/master/RELEASE_NOTES.md",
